Source: { "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Type":"Application", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1766867595", "Title":"QupZilla Web Browser", "FullDescription":"QupZilla is a new and very fast QtWebEngine browser. It aims to be a lightweight web browser available through all major platforms. This project has been originally started only for educational purposes. But from its start, QupZilla has grown into a feature-rich browser.<br> QupZilla has all standard functions you expect from a web browser. It includes bookmarks, history (both also in sidebar) and tabs. Above that, it has by default enabled blocking ads with a built-in AdBlock plugin.<br> <br> <b>Note</b>: starting from 2.2.6-1 version the application stopped skipping jail for gaining root rights. So if you are upgrading from an earlier version, you must execute<br> <tt>jailer -D -N -i com.nizovn.qupzilla</tt><br> for new version to work (the command should clean leftovers of previous root jailer configuration).<br><br>Changelog:<br>2.3.1: Fix a rotation issue.<br>2.3.0: Add reader mode, strip dead features, resolve crashes.<br>2.2.6-1: Switch to qt5sdk instead of skipping jail<br> 2.2.6-0: Upstream upgrade<br> 2.1.2-2: Split into separate packages, first Preware release, added support for context menus on long tap, added close button to window frames<br> 2.1.2-1: Experimental phone support, enabled support for plugins/proprietary-codecs<br> 2.1.2-0: Initial version", "Homepage":"https://gitlab.com/nizovn/qupzilla", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/qupzilla_icon.png", "Screenshots":[ "http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/screenshots/qupzilla_screenshot.png" ], "License":"GPL v3 Open Source", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.0", "DeviceCompatibility":["TouchPad","Touchpad Go"] }

