Source: { "Type":"OS Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1785357026", "Title":"TLS 1.3 Updates (TouchPad)", "FullDescription":"One-tap bundle of the safe webOS Archive modernization patches. Pulls in: modern OpenSSL 1.1.1w + TLS 1.2/1.3 for the browser, command-line curl, in-app WebKit (Mojo/Enyo), the mail client and the system Download Manager; updated Mozilla root certificates; NTP clock sync (so TLS certificate validity windows pass and apps work); the mojomail IMAP tag fix; the Help app redirect to help.webosarchive.org; and the Enyo App Catalog.<br><br>It also pulls two hardware-enablement packages that are not TLS fixes but are part of bringing the tablet up to date, both included by community request: <b>USB Settings</b> (USB host/OTG mode, high-power devices, USB storage mount/unmount, a live connected-device list and a USB reset -- for wired controllers, keyboards and flash drives) and <b>Bluetooth Gamepad Support</b> (pairs a DualShock 4 or other classic Bluetooth HID pad as a real gamepad). Between them, wired and wireless game controllers both work.<br><br>webOS 3.0.x (TouchPad) only. Does not install QupZilla, Atlas or LunaCE. The device reboots once at the end of the install.<br><br>Changelog:<br>1.0.10: require USB Settings 1.1.0 -- auto-arms the OTG controller to fix a first-cable-insert hang, adds a live connected-device list, and adds a USB Reset button.<br>1.0.9: require USB Settings 1.0.8 -- high-power mode now also configures controllers the port left unconfigured.<br>1.0.8: add Bluetooth Gamepad Support to the bundle.<br>1.0.7: add USB Settings.<br>1.0.6: add the Download Manager TLS package.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.0", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["TouchPad","Touchpad Go"], "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice" }

