Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "Title":"Browser TLS 1.3 (Phones)", "FullDescription":"<b>webOS 2.2.4 phones only -- HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2.</b> Not for the TouchPad, which has its own build. One package covers all three phones: it selects the right binaries at install time from the device board name and refuses to patch a device it does not recognise. Requires webOS 2.2.4 -- an un-upgraded Veer (2.2.0) or Pre 2 (2.1.0) is not supported.<br><br>Adds a process-private OpenSSL 1.1.1w + curl(zlib) under /usr/lib/ssl11 and points the stock webOS 2.2.4 phones (HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2) BrowserServer at it via RPATH, so the 2011 browser can reach modern TLS 1.2/1.3 sites. Requires a current /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt (Mozilla ca-certificates).", "License":"OpenSSL/curl", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/openssl_icon.png", "LastUpdated":"1785207389", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.2.4", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["Pre3", "Veer", "Pre2"] }

