Description: Modern TLS 1.2/1.3 for webOS apps (Mojo/Enyo WebKit) on webOS 2.2.4 phones (HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2)
Maintainer: WebOS Internals <support@webos-internals.org>
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "Title":"Luna TLS 1.3 (Phones)", "FullDescription":"<b>webOS 2.2.4 phones only -- HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2.</b> Not for the TouchPad, which has its own build. One package covers all three phones: it selects the right binaries at install time from the device board name and refuses to patch a device it does not recognise. Requires webOS 2.2.4 -- an un-upgraded Veer (2.2.0) or Pre 2 (2.1.0) is not supported.<br><br>Routes the app WebKit host (LunaSysMgr) through the OpenSSL 1.1.1w stack under /usr/lib/ssl11 so in-app HTTPS (Mojo/Enyo XHR, enyo.WebService) negotiates TLS 1.2/1.3. REQUIRES org.webosinternals.browser-tls13 (provides /usr/lib/ssl11). Edits the LunaSysMgr upstart launcher; REBOOT after install. Recovery: novacomd survives a UI failure -- restore /var/luna/LunaSysMgr.tls13-orig to /etc/event.d/LunaSysMgr and reboot.", "License":"OpenSSL/curl", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/openssl_icon.png", "LastUpdated":"1785207389", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.2.4", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["Pre3", "Veer", "Pre2"] }

