Filename: org.webosinternals.downloadmgr-tls13-phone_1.0.0_armv7.ipk
Description: Modern TLS 1.2/1.3 for the webOS Download Manager on webOS 2.2.4 phones (HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2) (downloads and uploads)
Maintainer: WebOS Internals <support@webos-internals.org>
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "Title":"Download Manager TLS 1.3 (Phones)", "FullDescription":"<b>webOS 2.2.4 phones only -- HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2.</b> Not for the TouchPad, which has its own build. One package covers all three phones: it selects the right binaries at install time from the device board name and refuses to patch a device it does not recognise. Requires webOS 2.2.4 -- an un-upgraded Veer (2.2.0) or Pre 2 (2.1.0) is not supported.<br><br>Routes the system Download Manager (com.palm.downloadmanager / /usr/bin/LunaDownloadMgr) on webOS 2.2.4 phones (HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2) through modern TLS so background downloads AND uploads reach today's HTTPS servers. LunaDownloadMgr does all its transfers via libcurl and links no OpenSSL directly, so it is simply RPATH'd (/usr/lib/ssl11dl:/usr/lib/ssl11) onto a modern libcurl 7.61.1 (OpenSSL 1.1.1w + c-ares + a baked-in CA bundle) -- no patch to the binary's code. The baked CA bundle is required because the daemon hard-codes an OpenSSL-0.9.8-hashed CAPATH that OpenSSL 1.1 cannot read. On the TouchPad this is hardware-proven (downloads negotiate TLS 1.3, modern/Let's Encrypt certificates validate, multipart uploads return 200). Bonus: downloads can now send arbitrary request headers (Authorization: Bearer <JWT>, X-Auth-Token, ...) via the cookieHeader multi-line convention (uploads already accept a customHttpHeaders array). REQUIRES org.webosinternals.browser-tls13 (provides /usr/lib/ssl11 OpenSSL); a current /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt (e.g. com.palm.rootcertsupdate) and a correct clock (org.webosinternals.ntpdate-sync) are needed for cert validation. Remove this BEFORE browser-tls13. No reboot needed.", "License":"OpenSSL/curl", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/openssl_icon.png", "LastUpdated":"1785207389", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.2.4", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["Pre3", "Veer", "Pre2"] }

