Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1785357026", "Title":"USB Settings", "FullDescription":"A Palm-style settings panel for the USB capabilities the TouchPad's OS hides.<br><br>Toggle <b>USB Host (OTG)</b> mode to use USB keyboards, game controllers and flash drives; enable <b>High-power devices</b> to run gear that draws more current than the port normally allows (such as a DualShock 4 over USB); and <b>mount / unmount USB storage</b> to browse a flash drive. Shows live status, a live list of connected devices (with icons for keyboard, mouse, gamepad and storage) while the panel is open, and posts a notification when a drive is detected, mounted or removed. A one-tap <b>USB Reset</b> recovers a device that stopped responding without a full reboot (refused while storage is mounted, so it can't yank a drive mid-use).<br><br>Self-contained: only uses capabilities and components already on the device, so it needs no other feeds. Adds no drivers, and there is no Bluetooth LE. Fully reversible.<br><br>Install <b>and uninstall via Preware / WebOS Quick Install</b>, then reboot. Do not use the launcher's Delete: it skips the cleanup script and would leave a background daemon running (the app hides its Delete button for this reason).<br><br>1.1.0: the OTG controller now arms itself automatically the first time the port is idle, fixing a hard hang some devices hit on their first-ever OTG cable insert; adds a live connected-device list with device-type icons; and adds a USB Reset button to recover a wedged connection.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.0", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["TouchPad", "Touchpad Go"], "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna", "License":"GPL", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/usbsettings-icon.png", "Screenshots":["http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/screenshots/usbsettings_screenshot.png"] }